  "Number": 8,
  "Question": "In the eight-term sequence \\(A,\\) \\(B,\\) \\(C,\\) \\(D,\\) \\(E,\\) \\(F,\\) \\(G,\\) \\(H,\\) the value of \\(C\\) is \\(5\\) and the sum of any three consecutive terms is \\(30.\\) What is \\(A + H?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(17\\)",
    "B": "\\(18\\)",
    "C": "\\(25\\)",
    "D": "\\(26\\)",
    "E": "\\(43\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "Two neighboring groups of three share two terms, so comparing their sums isolates the term that leaves and the term that enters. For example,\n\\[\nA+B+C=B+C+D=30\n\\]\ngives \\(A=D\\) after subtracting \\(B+C\\).\n\nApplying the same observation throughout the sequence gives\n\\[\nA=D=G,\\qquad B=E=H,\\qquad C=F.\n\\]\nThus \\(H=B\\), so the first three-term sum supplies exactly what we need:\n\\[\nA+H=A+B=30-C=30-5=\\boxed{25}.\n\\]\nThe answer is choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{C}}\\).",
